# MF Overhaul 0.3.41: user: "the ground particles appear in chunks like dust; they should look like they got sent violently up and
#   dissipate down". Re-reading c6: the clod rows carry 0;-9.8 (gravity) and exhaust 0;0.15, so c6 y is a vertical acceleration,
#   NEGATIVE = DOWN, positive = up. Earlier "lift" edits on smoke (-0.28/-0.24/-0.22) were therefore a slow sink; fixed here.
#   Thrown earth (dirt_expl / dirt_expl_big / dirt_bomb): launched harder (speed 0.6/0.5/0.45 -> 1/0.9/0.85), pulled down harder
#   (-5 -> -8) so it arcs and falls, and the sprites stay lumps instead of swelling into 10-18 m dust blobs (end 10/18/13 -> 5/8/7 m,
#   life 3.5/6/5 -> 3/4.5/4.5 s). Clods (ext_dirt) fly higher: speed 0.5 -> 0.8.
#   Burst smoke now rises: smoke_expl 0;+0.25, smoke_expl_big 0;+0.2, smoke_bomb 0;+0.18 (vanilla -0.1 settles).
# 7 operations
row~|parts_desc|dirt_expl|c6=v:0;-8|c10=v:5;5|c13=v:3;0;0.1;0.5|c14=f:1
row~|parts_desc|dirt_expl_big|c6=v:0;-8|c10=v:8;8|c13=v:4.5;0;0.1;0.6|c14=f:0.9
row~|parts_desc|dirt_bomb|c6=v:0;-8|c10=v:7;7|c13=v:4.5;0.1;0.1;0.7|c14=f:0.85
row~|parts_desc|ext_dirt|c14=f:0.8
row~|parts_desc|smoke_expl|c6=v:0;0.25
row~|parts_desc|smoke_expl_big|c6=v:0;0.2
row~|parts_desc|smoke_bomb|c6=v:0;0.18
